{"text": "Clty AND COUNTY OF SAN FRANCISCO OFFICE OF THE CITY ATTORNEY\n\nDENNIS J. HERRERA PEDER J. V. THOREEN\nCity Attorney Deputy City Attorney\nDirect Dial: (415) 554-3846\nEmail: Peder.Thoreen@sfcityatty.org\nMEMORANDUM\nPRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL\nTO: Sunshine Ordinance Task Force\nFROM: Peder J. V. Thoreen\nDeputy City Attorney\nDATE: \u2014 September 26, 2019\nRE: Complaint No. 19097: Anonymous v. Department of Public Works, Mohammed\n\nNuru, Jeremy Spitz\n\nCOMPLAINT\n\nAn anonymous complainant (\u201cComplainant\u201d) alleges that the Department of Public\nWorks (\u201cDPW\u201d), Director Mohammed Nuru, and Jeremy Spitz (collectively, \u201cRespondents\u201d),\nviolated the Sunshine Ordinance by failing to respond to Complainant\u2019s requests in a complete\nmanner.\n\nCOMPLAINANT FILES COMPLAINT\nOn September 9, 2019, Complainant filed this complaint with the Task Force, alleging\nthat Respondents violated Administrative Code sections 67.21, 67.26, and 67.27.\nJURISDICTION\nRespondents are subject to the Sunshine Ordinance. Respondents do no dispute\nJurisdiction.\nAPPLICABLE STATUTORY SECTION(S)\nSection 67 of the San Francisco Administrative Code:\ne Section 67.21 governs responses to a public records request in general.\ne Section 67.26 provides that withholding of public records shall be kept to a minimum.\ne Section 67.27 sets forth requirements for justifying the withholding of information.\nAPPLICABLE CASE LAW\ne None\nBACKGROUND\n\nOn August 23, 2019, Complainant submitted both immediate and regular disclosure\nrequests to the Department of Public Works, seeking four categories of documents: first, recent\nemails received by a variety of individuals on their government email accounts; second, recent\nemails sent from those email accounts; third, recent emails sent from those individuals\u2019 personal\n\nFox PLAZA + 1390 MARKET STREET, 7TH FLOOR - SAN FRANCISCO, CALIFORNIA 94102-5408\nRECEPTION: (415) 554-3800 - FACSIMILE: (415) 437-4644\n\nn:\\codenf\\as2019\\9600241\\01395220.docx",
